    "title": {
     "en": "A short story"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "Anu typed 2 + 3 x 4 into a calculator and got 14, not 20.\n\"Multiply first,\" said her teacher."
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "brackets",
     "order",
     "expression"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "When an expression has several operations we do brackets first, then multiplication and division from left to right, then addition and subtraction from left to right.\n2 plus 3 times 4 is 2 plus 12, which is 14. With brackets, (2 plus 3) times 4 is 20.\nBrackets can change the answer, so they must be placed carefully."
    }
   },
